-- §6.3 quiescence drain, DECLARED-scheme half of the `DrainDiags` population
-- (`compiler/types/typecheck.mdk`, #2705 / SA-10a item 17).
--
-- The twin of `s6-drain-quiescence-inferred-scheme.mdk`: here the receiver is
-- quantified by a WRITTEN signature (`nonlead`'s `(Ixd a b, Shb b) => …`) rather
-- than by an inferred one, and an unannotated relay carries it to graph end.  The
-- drain replays `Shb b` with `b` still an unbound `TVar` and
-- `routeUndeterminedTop`'s `_ => reportAmbiguousImpl` arm reports
-- `T-AMBIGUOUS-INSTANCE` on it (#3031).  Both halves matter because a fix that
-- consults only the binding's own inferred scheme would close one and leave the
-- other.
--
-- SPEC ANSWER, hand-derived before running anything: `main` calls the relay at
-- `b = Bool`, `a = Int`; `impl Shb Bool` and `impl Ixd Int Bool` are each the
-- unique match, `ixd` returns its first argument, so the program prints 7 on
-- every engine and `check` accepts.
--
-- WHAT THIS ROW PINS: `check` must NOT report `T-AMBIGUOUS-INSTANCE` — see the
-- sibling fixture's header for what a RED here means.
interface Ixd a b where
  ixd : a -> b -> a

impl Ixd Int Bool where
  ixd x _ = x

interface Shb a where
  shb : a -> a

impl Shb Bool where
  shb x = x

impl Shb Int where
  shb x = x

nonlead : (Ixd a b, Shb b) => b -> a -> a
nonlead n x = ixd x (shb n)

relay n x = nonlead n x

main = println (relay True 7)
